1 NOTE
2 CONT June 4, 1981 - Gilman H. Bjorgo, 69, of Decorah, Iowa, a retired farmer and construction worker, died Thursday night, May 28, 1981 in Winneshiek County Care Facility.  He had been ill for the past few months.  He was born June 30,
2 CONC  1911 in Allamakee County, Iowa a son of Elias and Julia (Halvorson) Bjorgo.  He was a lifelong area resident, excluding time spent in the military during WW II.  Educated in Allamakee County rural schools, he was a member of Big 
2 CONC Canoe Lutheran Church and American Legion Post 249 of Spring Grove.
2 CONT Survivors are two brothers, Roman of Minneapolis and Lloyd of Spring Grove.  Funeral services were at 1:30 p.m. Monday June 1st at Big Canoe Lutheran Church, Pastor Steve W. Jensen officiated.  Burial was in the church cemetery.
2 CONT Casket Bearers were:  Forrest Sacquitne, Charles Shuros, Obert Sacquitne, Jerome Kroshus, Lester Oefstedahl and Forrest Kroshus.  The Honorary pallbearers were:  Selmer Askelson, Walter Askelson, Bernard Shuros, Jens Shuros, Henry
2 CONC  Brunsvold and Carl Wernson.
