1 NOTE
2 CONT Martin emigrated to America in 1879.  For more than forty years he was a busy blacksmith at Highlandville, Iowa until about two years ago. Taken sick with cancer of the stomach forces him to quit his trade and about a year ago he 
2 CONC moved to Spring Grove, buying the Foss residence on Pleasant Avenue.  Funeral services were held at the home in Spring Grove on Sunday, July 13th and at the Big Canoe church of which he was a member. His eartly remains were laid t
2 CONC o rest in the Big Canoe Church cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Septembere 28, 1893 - Martin Peterson, the Highlandville blacksmith, was a business caller in Spring Grove, MN.
2 CONT
2 CONT March 26, 1896 - The well-known blacksmith from Highlandville, Iowa, spent Sunday with his brother Iver P. Seby of this village. (Spring Grove.)
2 CONT
2 CONT September 20, 1923 - Our jobbing department has printed auction bills for Martin Peterson, the sale to be held on Saturday September 22nd at his hold home in Highlandville, IA.  Mr. Peterson has bought the former A. A. Foss reside
2 CONC nce in Spring Grove and will soon make his home here.
1 CHAN
2 DATE 01 MAY 2022
